                      "Then Disney Parks pulled me onto their Special Projects skunkworks unit. That was the first time in my life I had ever wired a physical hardware breadboard. We wired RFID receivers, microcontrollers, and serial relays inside a hotel mock-up, proving that a guest could tap a wristband and have the room wake up with personalized lighting and itineraries. That breadboard prototype became the direct catalyst for Disney's multi-billion dollar <a href='/portfolio/my-disney-experience' class='text-lime underline font-medium'>MagicBand & MyMagic+ rollout</a>."
                    </p>
